<!--Post: 3081--><!--Time: 1104435844-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3081"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dawgar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dawgar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 11:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->does anyone know of a robbery at a wichitia sperm bank in the 70&#39;s?  I have heard this through the grape vine so to speak, but it would definately be of interest if it were true for the following reasons: <BR>sperm was found not in the victims, but around and possibably on the victims. <BR>although dna testing was not around at the time of the murders, he may have spread the sperm around to throw the profilers off base.  in other words the crimes may not have been sexual in nature and do to the predictability of sexual offenders that could cause the profilers to make incorrect assumptions. <BR>the btk&#39;s game plan tends to be to give enough false or misleading information as to guide the investigation away from the real killer, and to do it in an inconspicuous way. <BR>anyway just a thought.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3081-->
<!--Post: 3120--><!--Time: 1104469517-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3120"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 9:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I mentioned this idea in another thread. <BR> <BR>BTW: DNA testing wasn&#39;t done back then but blood typing was.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3120-->
<!--Post: 3131--><!--Time: 1104475863-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3131"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 10:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->That&#39;s very interesting. <BR> <BR>This brings up a related question - is all the DNA evidence coming from the sperm samples, or is there known to be confirmatory evidence from hairs, skin cells, etc., that might vouch for the BTK-ness of the sperm?  If there is no confirmatory DNA, then the simple possibility that he harvested some from a recurrent gay or male BDSM relationship needs to be looked at, to assure that the monetary and investigatory investment in DNA testing isn&#39;t being wasted.   Perhaps freeze/thaw or aging could be tested for in that case.  BTK was very careful with everything, and would likely have planned for blood type unless proven otherwise, in my opinion.  His &#34;factor X&#34; may have even been a poke at the cops about it.  Indeed, the real &#34;old bag trick&#34; &#40;allegedly mentioned in his letters&#41; may have been a sperm switcheroo. <BR> <BR>This guy is just lucky on everything.  The idea that he planned for blood type and got away with DNA would be par for the course.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3131-->
<!--Post: 3141--><!--Time: 1104502581-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3141"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dawgar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dawgar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 6:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->that was my concern as well ... <BR>good point about the old bag trick <BR>i did not think about that! <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3141-->
<!--Post: 3170--><!--Time: 1104539384-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3170"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bulldog87<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bulldog87<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 4:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yea i agree. I posted this on the 29 under the thread of new tech in 86. &#34;My thought was that if btk had been an MP, Forensic or medical background he might realize this as an effective way to throw off the investigation. Not neccessarily DNA, but blood type ect. &#40;he just lucked out on dna&#41; He could comfortably take the test and be eliminated as a suspect. This could be the reason why btk is so cocky and the investigators seem to struggle. I thought they got the DNA off of one specific crime scene, but I have no idea.&#34; I think this is biggest draw back from the police solving the case. they dont actually have BTK&#39;s DNA!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3170-->
<!--Post: 3185--><!--Time: 1104568184-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3185"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 01, 2005 - 12:29 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes, I see your post now, and concur completely.  Even a string of matching sperm samples isn&#39;t a sure thing, unless there&#39;s a match on something else, or there is strong circumstantial evidence to support authenticity.  Hopefully we&#39;re wrong. <BR> <BR>If you&#39;re right, then the police would need a powerful case on other evidence to part with their beloved DNA. <BR> <BR>I tend to believe that the police are &#40;now&#41; holding a good hand on DNA.  They should, and probably have, gone back to their evidence as new technology has made DNA workable with smaller and smaller samples.  So even if BLT did try a switcheroo, they would now know it, but would not let on, and could nail him in a moment of true surprise.  Just a thought &#40;and a hope&#41;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3185-->
<!--Post: 3186--><!--Time: 1104587120-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3186"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lucky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lucky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 01, 2005 - 5:45 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m thinking that if BTK is homosexual, he may have gotten all that DNA by other means.  Is there any evidence that he is gay?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3186-->
<!--Post: 3190--><!--Time: 1104599074-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3190"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dawgar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dawgar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 01, 2005 - 9:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->there is very circumstantial evidence that he may be sexually confused... <BR>first of all there is the &#34;x factor&#34; that he mentions, it may or may not have something to do with chromosomes...i doubt it but it is possible. <BR>also ...  it is thought he brought a change of clothes to the crime ...it could have been female clothing... <BR>next ...the psy drawings ...the first one looks like a regular guy ...the second&#40;how he looks when he commits the crime&#41; looks just like a female to me...and the third sketch looks like and old man...what he should look like now. <BR>this evidence is definately not solid but it is possible.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3190-->
<!--Post: 3215--><!--Time: 1104625699-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3215"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 01, 2005 - 4:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Please stay on track everyone... <BR> <BR><b>Sperm bank robbery</b> <BR> <BR>I&#39;d also like to learn details... <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3215-->
<!--Post: 3239--><!--Time: 1104650911-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3239"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 01, 2005 - 11:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sorry, Tom. <BR> <BR>I&#39;m not finding anything through Google, although the general idea may have been used in literature already: <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.dunno.com.au/booksdunno.html" target=_top>http://www.dunno.com.au/booksdunno.html</a> <BR> <BR>Sounds like a prime candidate for urban legend status.  We&#39;ll keep digging.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3239-->
<!--Post: 3240--><!--Time: 1104652283-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3240"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 01, 2005 - 11:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->...and here&#39;s an example of an urban legend:  <a href="http://www.snopes.com/humor/jokes/sperm.htm" target=_top>http://www.snopes.com/humor/jokes/sperm.htm</a> <BR> <BR>As one can see in the debunking here, it&#39;s much more trouble to pull off a true sperm heist than to simply pay for some in the right parts of town, if one only needs somebody else&#39;s.  Such a robbery would perhaps have motive if a very specific sperm is desired.  E.g., ex-husband&#39;s, dead husband&#39;s, dead fiance&#39;s, dead brother-in-law&#39;s, etc., as seen in various court cases. <BR> <BR>Alternate theory:  somebody, such as BTK, donated and wanted to withdraw the incriminating sample. <BR> <BR>I believe the truth of this rumor will need to be resolved by library work in Wichita - sorry I can&#39;t help there.  The auxilliary discussion &#40;BT-Gay?&#41; perhaps needs a new thread, folks...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3240-->
<!--Post: 4041--><!--Time: 1105558507-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4041"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Esau<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Esau<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 11:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The only problem with that theory is how could BTK know whether or not his or the sperm stolen was secretor type sperm that would show blood type? This guy is slick and I think the theory is very possible.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
